-## Storage
+## Storage and verification
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The cookie contains the member id and expiry as base64-encoded JSON, followed by an HMAC-SHA256 signature.
+It is signed, not encrypted. `sign()` creates it; `verify()` checks the signature and expiry and returns the
+member id, or `None` for a signature mismatch or an expired session. These functions live in
+[`larder/sessions.py`](../../larder/sessions.py).
+
+Every web server uses the same `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`, held in the deploy secrets. The module loads it at import time;
+if it is absent, the code falls back to `dev-only`, a development value rather than the deployment key.
+Sessions have no database table or per-request database lookup.
+
+## Revocation and key rotation
+
+The server cannot revoke one member's cookie before its expiry. There is no per-member revocation workaround;
+expiry follows the [lifetime rule](#lifetime). Rotating the shared key invalidates everyone's existing cookies,
+so the maintainers rotate it only between pickups. A deploy that retains the shared key preserves sessions.
 
